Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-25-99||07:12 PM||||Hey crew,<p>Any of you guys have any unique engine dress-up mods? custom made stuff,: rear sturt cover plates?, paint jobs, polished-up, etc.<p>What is that redish color??<p>Thanks
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-25-99||07:18 PM||||Shaun<br> I`ve looked all over for that red dist. cap. Can`t find it, what is the brand and the part no?, if you have it handy. Where did you get it?.  I thought that you said you ordered it.
Z||000002||DJRice||08-26-99||07:36 AM||||Your not going to beleive this, but I bought a distributor cap from Discount Auto parts last weekend, and when I opened up it was bright red.  I threw away the box but I'll go back and check the reciept to see if it has a brand.  It was only $10, and I got the red rotor to match for only $5.  I was not even hunting performance parts, I was just doing a tune up.  I need to go find some red plug wires now.<p>BTW, Discount Auto is a primarily SouthEast chain.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-26-99||04:40 PM||||I got my red cap from Autozone.
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||08-26-99||09:12 PM||||I might have to have you guys send me one. Any other red goodies you`ve found?
Z||000005||Shaun41178||08-26-99||09:58 PM||||Dad:  I bought my dist cap at Autozone.  It is made by Conrad industries and comes in a gold and black box.  The part number on the box is DR2012G and it comes with the rotor and brass terminals.  <p>I know you can get red wire covering.  you know the stuff that covers up all the wiring in the engine compartment and is black form the factory?  That stuff is available but is too much work for me to do that besides I am happy with it being black.<p>Russel makes hose sleeving kits that you can get at local auto parts store and are also in Summit and Jegs catalog.  These are sleeves that you put over the existing rubber hoses in your engien compartment and come with fittings color of your choice and it looks like you have metal lined hoses and such.  I don't think these are all that good looking but some people like them and is for dress up.  Expensive at around $45-$65 or so.<p>I have seen the rear strut covers and they werr chrome and the guy was at the MI Fiero show.  He is based out of Toledo where I am from but don't know how to get a hold of him or how much his products cost.<p>I have painted the muffler cover and cooling tubes to the coil and alternator a brite silver to help clean up the bay a little bit and it looks a lot better then the pitted metal when they are not painted even if they are clean.  Other then that I haven't done much in the detail dept of my engien bay although I do want it to look nice. 
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||08-26-99||10:21 PM||||Thanks Shaun,<p> I will hunt some more for the cap. We don`t have an auto zone out here (SSF) but I`ll check with the local speed shops.<p>
Z||000007||FieroGT||08-27-99||12:52 PM||||I also got red plug wires from Autozone. Nice fit, and only $16.99. Already had the silicone applied inside the plug boots and everything. No long-term reports yet, as I only have about 1500 miles on them. But, so far, so good!
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||08-30-99||08:07 PM||||Shaun, <p>Found a AutoZone I`ll be picking up that dist. cap over the weekend. Its a few miles away but, I`ll just make it a Saturday cruz.<p>Thanks for the info.<p>
